IMPORT prelude

-- Mishnah Kinnim: 3:2's "majority" AT A FIXED NUMBER OF OWNERS, with no list and no recursion.
-- Generated by tools/gen_fixed_arity.py (then tools/render.py); change the script, not this file.
-- Target compiler: main.
--
-- The text's own cases are fixed in size: 3:2 names five owners (one, two, three, ten and a hundred
-- pairs), and on Bartenura's reading it speaks of two women at a time.  kn-majority.l4 states Koppel's
-- and Reiss's smallest majority for any number of owners, over a list, and a solver takes no lists.
-- Here the same number is written out for two, three and five owners whose counts are anything: the
-- largest minority is the largest sum of some of the owners' pairs that is no more than half of all of
-- them, over every choice of owners; the smallest majority is all the pairs less it.
-- prove/kn-fixed-arity.l4 proves, for every count, that twice it is the fewest valid offerings over
-- every apportionment; kn-tests.l4 asserts that it equals the list form on the sources' cases.

§ `Kinnim 3:2 at a fixed number of owners`

{{Q mishnah-kinnim-3 8 13}}
@ref Kinnim 3:2 and its general principle, Koppel and Reiss, for a fixed number of owners (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:8-13)
GIVEN some IS A NUMBER
      all  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`so many pairs, if they are no more than half of all` some all MEANS
    IF (2 TIMES some) AT MOST all THEN some ELSE 0

§§ `Two owners`

GIVEN p1 IS A NUMBER
      p2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`all the pairs of two nests` p1 p2 MEANS
    p1 PLUS p2

-- Over all 3 choices of owners but all of them (all of them hold more than half).
@ref Kinnim 3:2, the general principle, second clause (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:13)
GIVEN p1 IS A NUMBER
      p2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest minority of two nests` p1 p2 MEANS
    max (max (`so many pairs, if they are no more than half of all` 0 (`all the pairs of two nests` p1 p2)) (`so many pairs, if they are no more than half of all` p1 (`all the pairs of two nests` p1 p2))) (`so many pairs, if they are no more than half of all` p2 (`all the pairs of two nests` p1 p2))

@ref Kinnim 3:2, the general principle, second clause (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:13)
GIVEN p1 IS A NUMBER
      p2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smallest majority of two nests` p1 p2 MEANS
    (`all the pairs of two nests` p1 p2) MINUS (`the largest minority of two nests` p1 p2)

§§ `Three owners`

GIVEN p1 IS A NUMBER
      p2 IS A NUMBER
      p3 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`all the pairs of three nests` p1 p2 p3 MEANS
    p1 PLUS p2 PLUS p3

-- Over all 7 choices of owners but all of them (all of them hold more than half).
@ref Kinnim 3:2, the general principle, second clause (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:13)
GIVEN p1 IS A NUMBER
      p2 IS A NUMBER
      p3 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest minority of three nests` p1 p2 p3 MEANS
    max (max (max (`so many pairs, if they are no more than half of all` 0 (`all the pairs of three nests` p1 p2 p3)) (`so many pairs, if they are no more than half of all` p1 (`all the pairs of three nests` p1 p2 p3))) (max (`so many pairs, if they are no more than half of all` p2 (`all the pairs of three nests` p1 p2 p3)) (`so many pairs, if they are no more than half of all` p3 (`all the pairs of three nests` p1 p2 p3)))) (max (max (`so many pairs, if they are no more than half of all` (p1 PLUS p2) (`all the pairs of three nests` p1 p2 p3)) (`so many pairs, if they are no more than half of all` (p1 PLUS p3) (`all the pairs of three nests` p1 p2 p3))) (`so many pairs, if they are no more than half of all` (p2 PLUS p3) (`all the pairs of three nests` p1 p2 p3)))

@ref Kinnim 3:2, the general principle, second clause (src:mishnah-kinnim-3:13)
GIVEN p1 IS A NUMBER
      p2 IS A NUMBER
      p3 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smallest majority of three nests` p1 p2 p3 MEANS
    (`all the pairs of three nests` p1 p2 p3) MINUS (`the largest minority of three nests` p1 p2 p3)

§§ `Five owners`

GIVEN p1 IS A NUMBER
      p2 IS A NUMBER
      p3 IS A NUMBER
      p4 IS A NUMBER
      p5 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`all the pairs of five nests` p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 MEANS
    p1 PLUS p2 PLUS p3 PLUS p4 PLUS p5

-- Over all 31 choices of owners but all of them (all of them hold more than half).
